B.dYj=new A.M("Skin","Your head holds your brain, eyes, ears, nose and mouth. It weighs about 5 kg, as much as a bag of sugar.")
B.e04=new A.M("Skin","You have about 100,000 hairs on your head. Each grows about a centimetre a month.")
B.dSE=new A.M("Senses","Your eyes turn light into signals for the brain. Each one sends the picture upside down and the brain flips it.")
B.dWq=new A.M("Senses","Ears hear sounds and also keep you balanced. The three tiny bones inside are the smallest in your body.")
B.e_U=new A.M("Senses","You can smell about a trillion different smells. Your nose also warms and cleans the air you breathe.")
B.dYu=new A.M("Senses","Your lips have lots of touch nerves and thin skin, which is why they are red.")
B.e2H=new A.M("Frame","Your neck holds your head up and carries the windpipe, food pipe, blood vessels and nerves.")
B.dZZ=new A.M("Cover","Your trunk holds your heart, lungs and digestive system, protected by skin, muscle and bone.")
B.dSN=new A.M("Movement","Each arm has 30 bones. Your elbow bends one way and your shoulder moves in almost any direction.")
B.e0o=new A.M("Touch","Each hand has 27 bones and thousands of touch sensors. Fingertips are some of the most sensitive spots.")
B.e1P=new A.M("Movement","Your legs have the biggest muscles and the longest bones in your body.")
B.e0P=new A.M("Balance","Each foot has 26 bones and about 125,000 sweat glands. Together they carry your whole weight.")
B.dRV=new A.M("Movement","These muscles turn and tilt your head. Your head weighs as much as a bowling ball, so they work all day.")
B.dZL=new A.M("Movement","A big kite-shaped muscle across your upper back that lifts your shoulders and moves your head.")
B.dZO=new A.M("Movement","The round caps of your shoulders. They lift your arms in every direction.")
B.dWL=new A.M("Movement","The chest muscles push your arms forward, like when you push a door.")
B.dUk=new A.M("Movement","The biceps bends your elbow. When a muscle works it gets shorter and fatter.")
B.dWa=new A.M("Movement","The triceps straightens your elbow. It works opposite the biceps: muscles can only pull, so they come in pairs.")
B.dZc=new A.M("Movement","Long muscles in your forearm pull on tendons that work your fingers, like puppet strings.")
B.e1h=new A.M("Movement","Your tummy muscles hold your body upright and help you bend and twist.")
B.e3q=new A.M("Movement","The muscles at the sides of your waist that help you twist and lean.")
B.e02=new A.M("Movement","The widest muscle in your back. It pulls your arms down, like when you swim or climb.")
B.dRJ=new A.M("Movement","Your bottom muscles are the biggest in your body. They push you up stairs and keep you standing.")
B.dZg=new A.M("Movement","Four muscles at the front of your thigh. Together they are the strongest in your body for lifting weight.")
B.dS8=new A.M("Movement","The muscles at the back of your thigh that bend your knee when you run.")
B.e1r=new A.M("Movement","The calf muscle pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.")
B.e1Z=new A.M("Movement","These lift your foot up so your toes do not drag on the ground.")
B.dZu=new A.M("Nerves","Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells and runs everything you do.")
B.e1A=new A.M("Hormones","A butterfly-shaped gland in your neck. It makes hormones that control how fast your body uses energy.")
B.dSG=new A.M("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.e2j=new A.M("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.dV2=new A.M("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.e17=new A.M("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.dWD=new A.M("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.dYq=new A.M("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.e0c=new A.M("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.e2s=new A.M("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.e2l=new A.M("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.e2o=new A.M("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.dYJ=new A.M("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
B.e0C=new A.M("Digestion","About 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. This is where most food is turned into energy for your blood.")
B.e0M=new A.M("Digestion","Takes the water from what is left and makes the rest into waste. It is about 1.5 metres long.")
B.e2c=new A.M("Cleaning","A stretchy bag that holds urine. It can hold about half a litre.")
B.dZt=new A.M("Nerves","A thick rope of nerves inside your backbone. It carries messages between your brain and the rest of your body.")
B.dXC=new A.M("Frame","Your skull is made of 22 bones that protect your brain. Only the jaw can move.")
B.dWZ=new A.M("Frame","The only bone in your skull that moves. You use it to chew, talk and smile.")
B.dZI=new A.M("Frame","Seven small bones called cervical vertebrae. A giraffe has seven too, just much longer!")
B.e08=new A.M("Frame","Twelve vertebrae that each hold a pair of ribs.")
B.dXT=new A.M("Frame","Five big, strong vertebrae that carry most of your upper body's weight.")
B.dYc=new A.M("Frame","The sacrum and coccyx. The tailbone is what is left of a tail from our far-off ancestors.")
B.dVc=new A.M("Frame","You have 12 pairs of ribs. They make a cage that protects your heart and lungs and moves when you breathe.")
B.e1Y=new A.M("Frame","The sternum is a flat bone in the middle of your chest that holds your ribs together at the front.")
B.dVC=new A.M("Frame","The most often broken bone, and the only long bone that lies sideways.")
B.dS6=new A.M("Frame","Two flat triangle bones on your back that let your arms swing in a big circle.")
B.dWK=new A.M("Frame",'The humerus. The bump at its end is the "funny bone": really a nerve that gets squashed.')
B.dS3=new A.M("Frame","Two bones, the radius and ulna, that twist round each other when you turn your hand over.")
B.dUz=new A.M("Frame","Eight small wrist bones plus the long bones of your palm and fingers: 27 in all.")
B.dWN=new A.M("Frame","The hip bones carry your body's weight and protect organs in your tummy.")
B.dVI=new A.M("Frame","The femur is the longest and strongest bone in your body, about a quarter of your height.")
B.e0l=new A.M("Frame","A small bone that shields your knee joint, like a built-in knee pad.")
B.dWi=new A.M("Frame","The tibia carries most of your weight below the knee. The thin fibula next to it helps hold the ankle steady.")
B.e3g=new A.M("Frame","Seven ankle bones and long toe bones. Your big toe is important for balance.")
B.dX1=new A.M("Blood","The biggest artery, about as wide as a garden hose. It carries fresh blood from the heart to the whole body.")
B.dYF=new A.M("Blood","The biggest vein. It brings used blood from the body back to the heart.")
B.e_2=new A.M("Blood","The carotid arteries take blood to your brain. You can feel your pulse here.")
B.dVL=new A.M("Blood","These carry blood to the lungs to pick up oxygen, and back to the heart.")
B.dVE=new A.M("Blood","Blood vessels that feed your legs. If you laid all your blood vessels end to end they would go round the Earth twice.")
